/**
 * data/b3/ordinals.js — the K-320 `ordinal-numbers` notation + word bank ×11.
 * EN block hand-authored (2026-09-14, the K-320 build session); the ten
 * non-EN blocks are GENERATED by tools/apply-b3-locale.js from
 * i18n/.draft-b3-<loc>.json after tools/validate-b3-draft.js (never hand-edit a
 * non-EN block here). Contract: docs/worksheet-gen/b3-designs/K-320-ordinal-numbers.md §5.
 * Read at render ONLY through lib/b3-common.js `bank('ordinals', loc)` /
 * `ordinalFor(loc, k, gender)`; data/b2/calendar.js ordinal() is NEVER called by
 * this type (it is a DATE style: es/pt/it `plain`, fr k > 1 bare).
 *
 * Per-locale block:
 *   notation      { 1..10: literal }  an EXPLICIT table, never a pattern (the
 *                 suffix system IS the learning: st/nd/rd/th, 1:a 2:a 3:e, º, e, .)
 *   notationF     feminine table — full in es/pt/it (U+00AA), { 1:'1re' } in fr,
 *                 null everywhere else (en: the notation has no gender)
 *   alt           accepted alternates, printed nowhere ({} when none)
 *   words         [{ k, m, f }] × 10, citation forms; f null where invariant
 *   capital       de: true only for the nominalised form (der Erste); else false
 *   genderPolicy  'position' (the answer is a PLACE: es/pt lugar m, it posto m,
 *                 fr rang m — one expected string per k) | 'noun' (F1 only)
 *   where         { label, printed } — F3's optional noun-free query label,
 *                 <= 30 chars, ends "?", no slot; printed:false by default
 *   wordPx        22 | 20 — set by the validator's measured worst 5-of-8 F2 row
 *   exemplar      the theme the type renders when no theme is pinned
 *   strings       per-face title + instruction (K-320 = the base; F1..F5 the
 *                 faces of §3) — the panel's authored copy; EN = the source the
 *                 panels audit. Noun-free by construction (no {noun}/{ordinal}
 *                 slot exists in this type) and free of relation words.
 *
 * EN glyph note: `º` U+00BA / `ª` U+00AA (es/pt/it) are carried by Baloo 2 700
 * (measured); `°` U+00B0 is BANNED everywhere (validator rule 1).
 */
